  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1903.01 Name Plate and Instruction Posting Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1903.01 Name Plate and Instruction Posting Requirements.\n\n(a) The owner or operator of an incinerator shall install the manufacturer’s name plate which lists the device’s model number and rated capacity and the types of waste for which the device is designed, in a conspicuous place on the device.\n\n(b) The owner or operator of an incinerator shall post detailed instructions for the operation of the device in a conspicuous place near the device.\n\nSource. #6483-B, eff 4-1-97 (formerly Env-A 1201); ss by #8294, eff 2-26-05; ss by #10317, eff 4-23-13 (from Env-A 1906.01); ss by #13697, eff 7-22-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1900.html"
